    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0292" n="180" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg180"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File 893.51/1923m</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-23T17:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 23, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Please communicate to the Foreign Office the substance of the Department’s
                    telegram of July 11, 4 p.m., and say that the American Government would be glad
                    to know that the Imperial Japanese Government agrees in principle to
                    cooperate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
